+## Hero build recipes (flat dots/rings/icons are the #1 low score)
+
+- **Size from the final camera state**: draw the hero so that after the push (centre + (x − centre)·S) it spans ≥ 55 % of
+  the width. Thin rings/bands/arrows get ≥ 60 px stroke, a gradient fill and a soft glow (blur copy at ≤ 0.35 alpha).
+  Icons in a crowd (ships, troops, drops) are ≥ 110 px, varied in size/rotation/bob, and cover the whole free area.
+- **Perspective, not a flat diagram**: a cone, ring, fleet or cloud deck is drawn with a vanishing point — rows shrink and
+  fade with distance, a near layer overlaps a far one (silhouette horizon, shore, mist), and the axis/source is visible.
+- **The camera keeps going to the last word**: pick start and end framings that differ (push toward the subject, then a
+  pull-out or pan for the reveal); never return to the start framing, never let the scene idle for the final third.
+- **Reveals use soft masks**: feather ≥ 80 px (gradient mask), never a hard rectangle edge; an end state must agree with
+  the narration (a full circle stays full, a retreating army visibly retreats).
+- **Cause → effect as a sequence**: source lights/moves first, then the effect travels item to item (fire hops along chains,
+  a light dot rides the ray path) and ends by tinting the whole scene.
